   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let g(x) = (x + 1) / ((x - 2) sqrt(20 + x - x^2)). Consider the largest interval that contains x = 0 and on which g is continuous. How many integers does that interval contain?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 5
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The square root sits in the denominator, so 20 + x - x^2 = (5 - x)(x + 4) must be strictly positive, giving -4 < x < 5, and the factor x - 2 also excludes x = 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               5,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               4
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "g is a quotient of a polynomial and a product of a polynomial with a square root function, each continuous on its domain, so g is continuous on (-4, 2) U (2, 5).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece containing x = 0 is (-4, 2), open at -4 because the denominator is zero there and open at 2.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in (-4, 2) are -3, -2, -1, 0 and 1.",
         "mathjson": 5
      }
   ],
